    {
      "type": "prose",
      "caption": "Summary",
      "html": "<p>This optional unit adds 50 words that occur 15–16 times in the New Testament and are not in Machen&#x27;s lessons: 23 nouns, 21 verbs and 6 other words. Nothing in the course waits for them; they are here so that you can read the New Testament with the lexicon open less often. Learn them on the Words track: recognize, recall, type, type with accents.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "caption": "Built from words you know",
      "html": "<p>These verbs are a preposition plus a verb from the lessons; the meaning usually follows from the parts: παρέχω (ἔχω); συλλαμβάνω (λαμβάνω); ἀπάγω (ἄγω); ἐπιμένω (μενῶ); προλέγω (λέγω); συμφέρω (φέρω).</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "caption": "Common confusion",
      "html": "<p>Look-alikes that differ by one letter: ἀπάγω (I lead) and ὑπάγω (I go away); δέρω (I flay) and φέρω (I bear); δεσμός (a bond) and δέσμιος (one bound); ὅθεν (whence) and πόθεν (whence); ὁμοιόω (I make like) and ὅμοιος (like). Feminine although they end in -ος, like ὁδός: Δαμασκός, παρθένος.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "caption": "Source",
      "html": "<p>Words chosen by their New Testament frequency (MorphGNT); glosses after Jeffrey Dodson&#x27;s Greek-English lexicon (public domain).</p>"
    },
